        "subject": "A payment reminder could not be sent",
        "emailType": "text",
        "message": "=The payment reminder to {{ $('Write the payment reminder').item.json.email }} could not be sent. Gmail said no, so it was not retried and the row (request {{ $('Write the payment reminder').item.json.request_id }}) says pay_failed in reply_label. Remind them yourself if they still owe you.",
        "options": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "name": "Tell the owner it failed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        1240,
        460
      ],
      "id": "8c034539-715e-4ab2-8fb1-a3e8aeff3f3e",
      "webhookId": "a5d551bf-29af-4afa-939a-9cbd9b2563e5"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send payment reminders for finished jobs from Google Sheets with Gmail\n\nFor service businesses that keep jobs in a Google Sheet and want a polite email, at most twice, to customers who have not paid.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every day at 10:00 it looks for rows with a date in `closed_at` (the day you finished or invoiced the job) that are not marked paid.\n2. The first reminder goes out 3 days after that date, the second 7 days after the first. Then it stops. Days and maximum are in **Settings**.\n3. Each email goes in the quote thread when `thread_id` is filled, as a new email if not. The row gets `pay_reminder_1` (or 2) and the date in `reply_label`.\n\nWhen the customer pays, type `paid` in `reply_label`. Rows with status `lost` or `no_reply` are skipped.\n\n### Setup\n1. Use the sheet described in the **Sheet** note.\n2. Pick your Google Sheets credential and paste your sheet URL in **Document** in **Read the sheet**, **Mark as reminded** and **Mark send failed**. Pick your Gmail credential in the two HTTP nodes and in **Tell the owner it failed**.\n3. Edit **Settings**: `business_name`, `owner_email` and `payment_info` (how to pay) first. Nothing is sent while they have the default values.\n4. Set Workflow settings > Timezone to the zone in `timezone`. Activate.\n5. By hand, when a job is done or invoiced, put a date like 2026-10-14 in `closed_at`.\n\nIf nothing happens, check **Executions**.\n\n### Requirements\n- Google Sheets and Gmail credentials in n8n: docs.n8n.io/integrations/builtin/credentials/google/. A Google Cloud app in Testing expires the connection after 7 days; publish it.\n- It does not know who paid. Mark `paid` before 10:00.\n\nOur paid template follows up Gmail quotes until the customer replies: https://payhip.com/b/OyN5V\n\nOne person is behind Small Hours. AI agents built and tested this template.",
